          "ts": "2026-10-05T11:39:28.985Z",
          "attempt": 1,
          "finding": "G4/G2 — align with 03-safety-guidelines.md, which now exists: (1) Running pain cap is 2/10 or less (not ~3/10); if pain exceeds 2/10, repeat or step back a week. (2) Once continuous jogging begins (any unbroken jog of 10+ min, currently week 6), total weekly jog minutes (A+B+C) may rise by no more than 10% per week; currently week 6->7 is about +24% (42->52) and 8->9 about +17% (54->63). Rebalance jog minutes between Days A/B and Day C so the 10% cap holds while Day C still builds to a continuous 5 km in week 10. (3) G2: make the week-10 Day C time math explicit with a pace consistent with your own estimate (25 min ≈ 3 km ≈ 8.3 min/km gives ≈ 42 min for 5 km); warm-up + 5 km + cool-down must be ≤ 45 min (e.g. 2 min brisk-walk warm-up and walking cool-down counted inside the limit, with a slow-jog start). State the pace needed for 5 km to fit. If a non-stop 5 km cannot fit in 45 min under these limits, say so plainly in the Summary instead of hiding it. Keep everything else unchanged."
        },
        {
          "ts": "2026-10-05T12:09:29.982Z",
          "attempt": 1,
          "finding": "G4: week 2→3 changes both jog block length and repeat count while blocks are ≤ 5 min (Days A/B: 3×(1j/2w) → 3j,2w,2j; Day C: 5×(2j/2w) → 5j,2w,5j,2w,4j). Rewrite week 3 (and week 4 if needed) so only ONE variable (block length OR repeat count) changes per day vs the previous week, per validation-report Finding 1; make the 'first continuous week' label match the safety definition (preferably keep week-4 blocks ≤ 5 min); keep the weeks 5-10 ≤10% chain and session caps (≤45 min, Day C weeks 9-10 ≤ 52/60 min exception)."
        }
