          "finding": "G2: Mon/Wed sessions planned at exactly 45.0 min assume ~45 s per work set, but reps × tempo run longer (box squat 12 reps with 3-s lowering ≈ 48-54 s; one-arm row 12/arm with 2-3 s lowering ≈ up to 48 s per arm; weeks 8-9 'reps up to 15 then 3-s tempo' ≈ 60 s), so real sessions are ≈ 45.3-47 min. Recompute every set from reps × tempo at the top of each rep range and bring every Mon/Wed session to ≤ 44 min (e.g. cut rest after the four main lifts from 60 s to 45 s, or use a weeks 8-9 progression that does not lengthen sets). Keep exercises 2642 and 1551, the 6:6 push:pull balance and the cardio blocks unchanged. Make the weekly volume range a single consistent value (text says 4-8 sets, table says 4-9)."
